From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:28:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the copy batch index only where the assertion reads it

The partitioned COPY task builder keeps the batch index its collection
slot returns only to assert that it matches the task's, so in a
release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the index is
unused and -Wunused-variable says so. The slot is still added in every
build; the index is bound and asserted on only when assertions are
enabled, which is the shape upstream gives the site later.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/persistent/physical_copy_to_file.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/persistent/physical_copy_to_file.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/persistent/physical_copy_to_file.cpp
index 2bd27d1413..8fb0b22487 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/persistent/physical_copy_to_file.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/persistent/physical_copy_to_file.cpp
@@ -1050,9 +1050,13 @@ optional<PartitionedCopyTask> PartitionedCopyHashGroup::TryNextBatchTask() {
 	task.end_idx = batch_row_idx;
 
 	// Update partition/batch counters
+#ifdef D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED
 	const auto batch_idx =
 	    batch_state.AddCollectionSlot(partitioned_copy.GetPartitionCollectionSchema(), task.end_idx - task.begin_idx);
 	D_ASSERT(batch_idx == task.batch_idx);
+#else
+	batch_state.AddCollectionSlot(partitioned_copy.GetPartitionCollectionSchema(), task.end_idx - task.begin_idx);
+#endif
 
 	return task;
 }
